with the \(\tau=263\pm 2\) ps compiled by the Particle Data Group [10]. There have been several measurement results of \({}^{3}_{\Lambda}\)H lifetime till now. We summarize the lifetime values from all the measurements till now in the right panel of Fig. 3.

## 4 Summary

We present the STAR preliminary analysis on \({}^{3}_{\Lambda}\)H production in RHIC Au+Au collsions at \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{\rm NN}}^{{}^{\ast}}}=7.7\), \(11.5\), \(19.6\), \(27\), \(39\), and \(200\) GeV. The combined \({}^{3}_{\Lambda}\)H + \({}^{3}_{\Lambda}\)\(\overline{\rm H}\) signal is obtained with \(9.6\sigma\) significance. The beam energy dependence of strangeness population factor \({}^{3}_{\Lambda_{\Lambda}\Lambda_{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{ \rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{\rm{                  }}}}}}}}}}}}}\) is presented and the result indicates that S\({}_{3}\) increases with increasing beam energy with \(1.7\sigma\) significancy. A statistically improved \({}^{3}_{\Lambda}\)H lifetime: \(123\pm^{26}_{22}(stat)\pm 10(sys)\) ps, is also presented.

